    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Completeness</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Completeness dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Does the article contain enough information for an agent to answer the question? Checks title, summary, data categories, and body depth.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Structure</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Structure dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Is the article formatted so a retrieval model can chunk it cleanly? Checks headings, length, Q&amp;A form, links, and orphaned lists.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Clarity</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Clarity dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>How easily an agent can understand the article. Checks jargon, passive voice, and ambiguous pronouns (this, that).</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Freshness</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Freshness dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>How recently the article was updated. Older articles risk containing outdated information — this score decays with age.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Duplication</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Duplication dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Does this article overlap with others in the KB? Scored from the deduplication pipeline — articles with near-duplicates score lower.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Dim_Conflict</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring-dimension</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Conflict dimension helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Does this article contradict another in the KB? Scored from the deduplication pipeline — contradictions confuse agents and lower the score.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Overall_Score</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,scoring</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Overall readiness score helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Weighted 0–100 score across all 6 scoring dimensions. 80+ is Ready, 50–79 is Needs Work, below 50 is Not Ready.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_Contains</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Contains operator helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Matches articles where the field value includes the search term anywhere (case-insensitive).</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_StartsWith</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Starts With operator helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Matches articles where the field value begins with the search term (case-insensitive).</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_Equals</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Equals operator helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Matches articles where the field value is exactly the search term.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_DateGte</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Date greater-or-equal operator helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Matches articles where the date is on or after the given date. Use ISO format: YYYY-MM-DD.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_DateLte</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Date less-or-equal operator helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Matches articles where the date is on or before the given date. Use ISO format: YYYY-MM-DD.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_LogicAnd</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Clause logic AND helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Article must match all added clauses. Stricter — returns fewer results.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Filter_LogicOr</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,article-selector</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Clause logic OR helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Article matches if any clause matches. Broader — returns more results.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_DataCloud</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Data Cloud helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Data Cloud powers semantic vector search for higher-quality deduplication. Without it, the pipeline falls back to SOQL keyword matching.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_SearchIndex</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Search index helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Data Cloud vector search requires a configured search index name. Set this in Step 4 — Runtime &amp; Retrieval.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_ContentFields</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Content fields helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>The scorer reads article body from the fields you select. Without at least one content field, articles cannot be scored.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_ArticlesExist</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Articles exist helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>At least one published article is needed for an assessment run to produce results.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_BypassPermission</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Bypass permission helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Bypass_AI_Knowledge_Check lets trusted authors publish without running the sidebar consistency checker. Optional.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Preflight_ContentFieldsMatchIndex</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,preflight</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Preflight: Content fields match index helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Dimension scoring reads the content fields you select in Step 2; the dedup pipeline reads whatever the search index embeds. A mismatch means the two surfaces evaluate different text — a soft warning, not a blocker.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_MaxFinalists</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Max finalists helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Upper bound on how many duplicate candidates each article can produce. Higher finds more matches but costs more LLM calls.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_MaxChunks</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Max chunks helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Number of body-text chunks per article fed into vector search. Higher improves recall, increases Data Cloud consumption.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_TopK</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Top K helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>How many nearest neighbors vector search returns per query. Higher improves recall but grows downstream work.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_SimThreshold</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Similarity threshold helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Minimum chunk-level cosine similarity (0–1) a semantic-search match must clear to be kept as a duplicate candidate. This is an embedding-retrieval cutoff — NOT the article-level Confidence Score shown on candidates in the Action Center (that is an LLM judgment on a 0–100 scale). Higher = fewer false positives but more missed duplicates. Default 0.75.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_Languages</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Supported languages helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Comma-separated locale codes (e.g. en_US, fr) the pipeline will process. Articles in other languages are skipped.</value>
    </labels>
    <labels>
        <fullName>KB_Helptext_Pipeline_MaxChunkSize</fullName>
        <categories>kb-readiness,helptext,pipeline-config</categories>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <shortDescription>Pipeline: Max chunk size helptext</shortDescription>
        <value>Maximum characters per text chunk during agentic duplicate analysis. Default 500. Larger chunks give more context, smaller chunks give more granular matches.</value>
    </labels>
